{
    "background_story": "Giuliana was a passionate Italian chef who owned a quaint trattoria in the heart of Tuscany. Her culinary creations were renowned for their bold flavors, and one ingredient stood out as her signature touch: garlic. Giuliana's love affair with garlic began in her childhood, watching her nonna expertly chop and saut\u00e9 cloves to bring out the depth in her sauces. As a chef, Giuliana experimented with various garlic varieties, from the pungent Silverskin to the sweet and nutty Elephant garlic. Her menu boasted an array of garlic-infused dishes, from classic spaghetti aglio e olio to innovative garlic-crusted pizzas. Regulars at the trattoria would often joke that Giuliana's cooking had the power to ward off vampires, thanks to the generous amounts of garlic in every recipe. Her dedication to the humble bulb earned her the nickname 'La Regina dell'Aglio' \u2013 The Garlic Queen.",
